# Example of an OpenSSH allowed-signers file for the "only signed tags" mode.
# This file holds NO real key: the line below is a placeholder that does not verify anything.
#
# Format, one line per trusted key:
#   <principal> namespaces="git" <key type> <base64 public key> [comment]
#
# The fingerprint of a key is shown by `ssh-keygen -lf key.pub`, for example:
#   256 SHA256:EXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLE000 release signing (ED25519)
# The SHA-256 of THIS FILE (sha256sum allowed_signers) is what the updater setting
# "allowed_signers_sha256" pins; change a line and the pin must change on purpose.
release-signer@example.invalid namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLEEXAMPLE
